## Strategy C — Codex: `codex mcp add` before spawn, `codex mcp remove` after

Codex has no project-level config or per-run flag. MCP servers must be registered via the `codex mcp` CLI. Use a local boolean to track registration state rather than mutating the function parameter.

Modify `spawnCodex()` to accept `mcpServerUrl?: string | null` as its last parameter.

Before spawning the child process:
```typescript
let codexMcpRegistered = false;
if (mcpServerUrl) {
  try {
    execSync(`${CODEX_BIN} mcp add playwright --url ${mcpServerUrl}`, { stdio: 'pipe' });
    codexMcpRegistered = true;
    process.stdout.write(`[BrowserMCP] Registered playwright MCP in codex config\n`);
  } catch (e: unknown) {
    const msg = e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e);
    process.stdout.write(`[BrowserMCP] WARNING: Failed to register playwright MCP in codex: ${msg}\n`);
    // codexMcpRegistered stays false — cleanup will be skipped
  }
}
```

In the `'exit'` event handler (the handler that calls `resolve({...})`), add cleanup as the final action before the resolve call:
```typescript
if (codexMcpRegistered) {
  try {
    execSync(`${CODEX_BIN} mcp remove playwright`, { stdio: 'pipe' });
  } catch { /* ignore if already gone */ }
}
```

