## Backend: POST /api/pipeline/preflight (backend/src/routes/pipeline.ts)

The preflight handler is at around line 929. Add `browserMcpAvailable` to the response.

Use `require.resolve()` to check if @playwright/mcp is installed — this is the correct approach as it checks node_modules resolution without spawning a process or relying on a --version flag (which @playwright/mcp does not support):

```typescript
let browserMcpAvailable = false;
try {
  require.resolve('@playwright/mcp');
  browserMcpAvailable = true;
} catch {
  browserMcpAvailable = false;
}
```

