The spec's `browserMcp` flag lives in the `detail` variable (typed as `SpecDetailData`, which has `[key: string]: unknown` catch-all), NOT in the `summary` prop (which is typed as `SpecSlideOverSummary` and does not have this field). Access it as `(detail?.browserMcp as boolean) === true`.

In the spec header metadata row (around line 660, in the same `<div>` that shows the model badge and time), add a purple Browser MCP badge:
```tsx
{(detail?.browserMcp as boolean) === true && (
